  "pitfalls": [
    "Amounts are read in report sign: revenue and costs both positive. Ledger extracts that store credits as negatives show negative revenue; flip credit balances before upload.",
    "Subtotal rows (gross profit, EBITDA, total expenses, net income) must be removed; summed with the detail lines they double count.",
    "Margins and ratios are recomputed from totals for each period and cost centre; averaging monthly margins overweights small months.",
    "A budget variance means different things by line: actual above budget is good for revenue and bad for costs. Revenue vs budget and Cost vs budget carry the sign; read the raw variance with an account-type filter.",
    "Account types not recognised as revenue or other income are treated as expenses in net income; check Value meanings in Check & map so every type is assigned.",
    "Balance-sheet items (cash, receivables, payables, loans) are point-in-time balances and must never be summed across months; this template covers P&L flows and invoice-level receivables and payables."
  ]
